273
00:11:43,662 --> 00:11:45,122
I'm coming with you.

274
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:46,915
Why are you wearin' my helmet?

275
00:11:47,124 --> 00:11:49,835
I don't expect this to end well.

276
00:11:50,085 --> 00:11:51,211
And the pillows?

277
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:52,713
Same answer.

278
00:11:54,047 --> 00:11:55,507
Turn it off.
I've got to concentrate.

279
00:11:55,716 --> 00:11:57,009
Aw.

280
00:11:57,384 --> 00:11:58,969
Okay,

281
00:11:59,178 --> 00:12:00,387
seat belts, everybody.

282
00:12:01,305 --> 00:12:02,764
Please drive slowly.

283
00:12:02,973 --> 00:12:04,850
Relax. I know what I'm doin'.

284
00:12:05,893 --> 00:12:07,060
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

285
00:12:07,269 --> 00:12:08,663
Adult Sheldon:
I've often been asked

286
00:12:08,687 --> 00:12:10,981
why I never learned
to drive a car.

287
00:12:11,190 --> 00:12:12,190
This night...

288
00:12:13,942 --> 00:12:15,277
Is your answer.

289
00:12:15,819 --> 00:12:17,154
Please slow down.

290
00:12:17,362 --> 00:12:18,562
I'm goin' eight miles an hour.

291
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:20,157
A cow just passed us.

292
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:22,951
- Do you know how to get to the hospital?
- Yeah.

293
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:25,120
It's right across the street
from the dairy queen.

294
00:12:25,162 --> 00:12:26,580
Which dairy queen?

295
00:12:26,788 --> 00:12:27,998
What are you talkin' about?

296
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:29,249
There's two.

297
00:12:29,625 --> 00:12:30,250
Really?

298
00:12:30,459 --> 00:12:31,126
You're gonna hit it!

299
00:12:31,335 --> 00:12:32,615
Which is the one
mom takes us to?

300
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:33,669
You're gonna hit it!

301
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,842
Ooh, you're in trouble now!

302
00:13:03,158 --> 00:13:04,158
Yeah?

303
00:13:04,618 --> 00:13:06,203
What took you so long to answer?

304
00:13:06,411 --> 00:13:08,538
Powdering my nose.
What's it to ya?

305
00:13:09,414 --> 00:13:11,750
Sorry I asked. Just wanted
to give you an update.

306
00:13:12,334 --> 00:13:14,127
Y... what's goin' on?

307
00:13:14,586 --> 00:13:16,046
They want to run
some more tests.

308
00:13:16,255 --> 00:13:17,839
They're gonna hold him
overnight.

309
00:13:18,048 --> 00:13:20,926
Oh. Oh, well, that's, that's
nothin' to worry about.

310
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,552
That's just precautionary.

311
00:13:23,262 --> 00:13:24,262
How are the kids?

312
00:13:24,429 --> 00:13:26,223
Oh. They were a little worried,

313
00:13:26,431 --> 00:13:28,600
but I handled it.

314
00:13:28,892 --> 00:13:29,893
They sleepin'?

315
00:13:30,143 --> 00:13:31,186
Um...

316
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:34,106
Yeah, yeah.

317
00:13:34,356 --> 00:13:35,399
You bet.

318
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:37,484
Thanks again for helpin'.

319
00:13:37,693 --> 00:13:38,693
Oh, hey,

320
00:13:38,819 --> 00:13:40,153
these are my grandchildren.

321
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:42,114
They are my blood.

322
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:43,740
Okay. I better go.

323
00:13:43,949 --> 00:13:46,618
Okay. We 71 talk later.

324
00:13:59,881 --> 00:14:01,008
Son of a bitch.

325
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:05,429
I hate those kids.

326
00:14:05,637 --> 00:14:08,932
Jj

327
00:14:09,349 --> 00:14:11,059
Missy:
Just admit it, we 're lost.

328
00:14:11,310 --> 00:14:12,477
We're not lost.

329
00:14:12,686 --> 00:14:14,730
Well, I sure don't see
a hospital anywhere.

330
00:14:15,105 --> 00:14:17,190
Why don't we ask somebody
for directions?

331
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:19,693
Because we're children
in a car, genius.

332
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,070
Dang it!

333
00:14:22,279 --> 00:14:23,947
Are you aiming for them?

334
00:14:24,156 --> 00:14:25,949
Everybody just shut up.
I got this.

335
00:14:29,202 --> 00:14:31,955
Oh, no. We're going to jail.

336
00:14:32,164 --> 00:14:33,582
Georgie's going to jail.

337
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:35,292
I'm saying I was kidnapped.

338
00:14:35,876 --> 00:14:36,894
Sheldon: That's a good plan.

339
00:14:36,918 --> 00:14:38,462
You and I were kidnapped.

340
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:41,006
If I'm going to jail,
we're all going to jail.

341
00:14:41,590 --> 00:14:44,217
Oh, you better pull over.

342
00:14:48,764 --> 00:14:50,140
George Jr.: Oh, thank god.

343
00:14:50,474 --> 00:14:52,726
- Well, don't just sit there... follow it.
- Why?

344
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:55,187
It's an ambulance...
It's going to the hospital.

345
00:14:56,438 --> 00:14:57,481
Hang on.

346
00:15:00,984 --> 00:15:03,111
Missy: How about I put
the radio on real low?

347
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:04,446
George Jr.: Shut up.

348
00:15:06,239 --> 00:15:07,239
Mary.

349
00:15:07,324 --> 00:15:07,949
Mom!

350
00:15:08,158 --> 00:15:09,951
- Where are they?
- Where's who?

351
00:15:10,869 --> 00:15:12,204
More importantly...

352
00:15:15,457 --> 00:15:16,958
How is George? Sheldon: -Mom!

353
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:19,503
- Ah. There they are!
- Hey. Oh.

354
00:15:19,711 --> 00:15:21,147
Meemaw: Ha! I lost
the little rascals

355
00:15:21,171 --> 00:15:22,881
in the... hall.

356
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:24,590
I want to see dad.

357
00:15:24,716 --> 00:15:25,716
- Me, too.
- Me, too.

358
00:15:25,801 --> 00:15:26,968
The doctors are with him now.

359
00:15:27,177 --> 00:15:28,303
I'll take you in a bit.

360
00:15:28,512 --> 00:15:29,721
Why are they here?

361
00:15:30,347 --> 00:15:31,765
I think it's obvious.

362
00:15:32,015 --> 00:15:33,266
They love their daddy.

363
00:15:33,517 --> 00:15:36,436
No, I get that.
Why aren't they home in bed?

364
00:15:41,483 --> 00:15:43,193
Well, nobody could sleep.

365
00:15:43,819 --> 00:15:45,445
I thought it was
the right thing.

366
00:15:48,115 --> 00:15:48,782
Good bluff.

367
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:50,075
Shh.

368
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:52,160
Okay, thank you.

369
00:15:52,411 --> 00:15:53,829
You all need anything?
You hungry?

370
00:15:54,037 --> 00:15:55,038
- No.
- No, th nk you.

371
00:15:55,247 --> 00:15:56,957
Okay, everybody sit tight.

372
00:15:57,165 --> 00:15:59,084
I'm gonna go check on your dad.

373
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:02,628
Georgie.

374
00:16:04,005 --> 00:16:05,090
Give me my damn keys.

375
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:07,676
Oh, yeah. Here.

376
00:16:08,635 --> 00:16:09,635
Thank you.

377
00:16:11,388 --> 00:16:12,806
How did I beat you here?

378
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:15,058
We kept hitting garbage cans.

379
00:16:15,267 --> 00:16:16,268
Oh, god.

380
00:16:16,852 --> 00:16:17,978
I need to wash my hands.

381
00:16:18,186 --> 00:16:21,273
- There are germs here that can kill you.
- Hold up.

382
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:24,317
Now, y'all like it
when your meemaw babysits.

383
00:16:24,526 --> 00:16:26,820
Poker, candy, firecrackers.

384
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:28,447
- Yes. - Yeah.
- Yeah.

385
00:16:28,655 --> 00:16:30,490
Well, if your mother
ever finds out

386
00:16:30,782 --> 00:16:32,200
what you did tonight,

387
00:16:32,409 --> 00:16:34,786
that is never
gonna happen again.

388
00:16:34,995 --> 00:16:36,413
I can't lie to my mother.

389
00:16:36,621 --> 00:16:39,332
Sure you can.
Believe in yourself!

390
00:17:35,138 --> 00:17:37,015
Jj

391
00:17:48,568 --> 00:17:50,208
Adult Sheldon:
Despite what it looks like,

392
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:52,155
I didn't pray to god that night.

393
00:17:52,364 --> 00:17:54,866
[Prayed to Blaise Pascal.

394
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,535
My thinking was,

395
00:17:56,743 --> 00:17:59,246
if he was right
about the existence of god,

396
00:17:59,454 --> 00:18:01,122
then he could pass along
my request

397
00:18:01,331 --> 00:18:02,916
for my dad to get better.

398
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:05,085
If he was wrong...

399
00:18:05,794 --> 00:18:06,794
Well...

400
00:18:07,254 --> 00:18:10,215
In this moment,
I needed him to be right.

401
00:18:16,263 --> 00:18:17,514
What's taking so long?

402
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:18,390
Shh.

403
00:18:18,598 --> 00:18:20,684
Keep your voice down, car thief.

404
00:18:20,892 --> 00:18:23,270
I didn't steal your car,
I just borrowed it.

405
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:26,189
You're gonna need
to make bail someday.

406
00:18:26,606 --> 00:18:29,734
Do not come to me.

407
00:18:30,277 --> 00:18:30,902
Mary: Good news!

408
00:18:31,111 --> 00:18:32,320
Your daddy's gonna be fine.

409
00:18:32,529 --> 00:18:34,739
- Should be home in a day or two.
- Oh!

410
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:36,116
And was it a heart attack?

411
00:18:36,324 --> 00:18:37,659
Minor. No permanent damage.

412
00:18:37,909 --> 00:18:39,995
Oh! That's wonderful!

413
00:18:40,203 --> 00:18:41,830
Our prayers have been answered.

414
00:18:43,331 --> 00:18:43,957
Come on, everybody,

415
00:18:44,165 --> 00:18:45,875
let's say hello to your old dad.

416
00:18:46,084 --> 00:18:47,794
Jj

417
00:18:48,378 --> 00:18:49,378
Come on.

418
00:18:50,088 --> 00:18:51,274
Adult Sheldon:
For a brief moment,

419
00:18:51,298 --> 00:18:54,467
I was filled with
the healing power of faith.

420
00:18:55,552 --> 00:18:57,721
Then the next day,
we all got violently ill

421
00:18:57,929 --> 00:19:00,849
from Billy sparks' eggs,
and I was over it.

422
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:08,356
I thought I'd talk this morning
about how it all began.

423
00:19:08,690 --> 00:19:11,651
Now, everybody knows how,
on the first day of creation,

424
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:14,112
god said, "let there be light."

425
00:19:14,404 --> 00:19:15,697
And there was light.

426
00:19:15,905 --> 00:19:19,159
And when god saw that light,
he knew it was good.

427
00:19:20,702 --> 00:19:21,702
Oh, here we go.

428
00:19:22,370 --> 00:19:23,413
Yes, Sheldon.

429
00:19:23,622 --> 00:19:26,833
You said he didn't create
the sun until day four.

430
00:19:27,208 --> 00:19:27,876
Yeah.

431
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:30,378
So how could there be light
the first three days?

432
00:19:30,629 --> 00:19:32,172
God is light.

433
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:33,840
So god's a photon?

434
00:19:36,843 --> 00:19:38,219
God's what made photons
possible.

435
00:19:38,428 --> 00:19:40,180
And what day did he do that?

436
00:19:40,472 --> 00:19:41,806
I would think day one.

437
00:19:42,307 --> 00:19:44,787
If I grab my chest and keel over,
maybe we can get out of here.

438
00:19:44,851 --> 00:19:46,519
That's a terrible thing to say.

439
00:19:46,728 --> 00:19:48,563
Because the first day
had just begun.

440
00:19:48,772 --> 00:19:50,190
So, before the big bang?

441
00:19:50,398 --> 00:19:51,608
There was no big bang.

442
00:19:51,816 --> 00:19:53,151
There was only the word.

443
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:55,153
Was the word "kaboom"?

444
00:19:55,403 --> 00:19:56,571
Okay, do it.

445
00:19:57,739 --> 00:19:58,739
We gotta go.

446
00:20:00,367 --> 00:20:01,451
Missy: What's happening?

447
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:03,536
- Is it over?
- Y-Yes.

